      "description": "Lead backend Java engineer for the HelixIPLM team, an IP Lifecycle Management platform. Since Helix IPLM was acquired by Perforce in 2020, continued to contribute in the same team with additional responsibilities.\n\n⭐️ Founding engineer of the Public RESTful API. Designed, implemented, tested, and maintained internal and customer facing documentation. Main point of contact for troubleshooting, debugging, and providing root cause analysis for customer support incidents.\n⭐️ Collaborated closely with Product Owner to analyze new requirements' impact on existing features and to architect the API and database schema for the Planning IP feature which enabled customers to seamlessly interact with the existing tool to reuse production IPs during brainstorming and design phase.\n⭐️ Architected, designed, developed, and maintained documentation for Jira plugin bug tracking system, an end-to-end plugin that synchronized Jira bug tickets and affected IPs in the IPLM platform which significantly improved customer's development productivity and traceability.\n⭐️ Led a team of four senior engineers. Conducted code reviews focusing on optimized, efficient, and maintainable code enforcing SOLID engineering best practices. Prioritized business needs and team member's expertise to deliver a high quality product and maintain a highly motivated team.\n⭐️ Hired, onboarded, and trained three classes of software engineer interns.\n\nProgramming Language: Java, Python, Neo4j Cypher Query",
      "insights": "Java Development, REST APIs and +3 skills"
